    <http://example.org/activity/activity9> a prov:Activity ;
        prov:startedAtTime "2026-05-26T14:59:46"^^xsd:dateTime ;
        prov:wasAssociatedWith <http://example.org/node/orchestrator> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given The City of Belval requirements, I would recommend using the Agile Scrum methodology for this tender. using will allow for flexibility, iterative development, and continuous improvement, which are essential for integrating into existing practices and providing intelligent assistance. our company's past public sector references, such as the digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia, demonstrate our company's ability to deliver complex projects in the public sector. These experiences can be leveraged to inform our company's approach and ensure a coherent bid response. To enhance our company's bid, our company's could consider partnering with consortium partners like EuroCloud Solutions S.A. for sovereign cloud hosting, LexIA GmbH for legal AI and regulatory compliance, or GreenCompute S.r.l. for green IT and energy-efficient infrastructure. partnering would enable our company's to provide a comprehensive solution that addresses The City of Belval environmental and energetic consumption concerns. our company's available capacity, with 60% of project management capacity available, allows our company's to take on this tender without overcommitting our company's resources. our company's can ensure a coherent bid response by emphasizing our company's ability to deliver a tailored solution that meets The City of Belval specific needs, leveraging our company's past experiences and consortium partners' expertise." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of governance practices, our company's can propose a structured approach using our company's typical delivery structure, which includes phases like Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. our company's will also utilize governance tools such as RAID logs, decision logs, and change request processes to ensure transparency and effective communication throughout this tender. By highlighting our company's Agile Scrum methodology, past public sector experiences, consortium partners, available capacity, and robust governance practices, our company's can submit a strong bid that demonstrates our company's ability to deliver a successful project for The City of Belval." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide times of response lower than 2 seconds, guarantee high availability (99.9%), integrate with existing systems (civil status, town planning, EDM, user directories), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU. No dependency on non-European suppliers is allowed. Can our current technology stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do you propose to ensure seamless integration and high performance? our current technology stack can meet the requirements of response times lower than 2 seconds and high availability of 99.9%. our typical performance benchmarks show a p95 response time of 1800 ms which is below the required threshold, and our have achieved an availability of 99.92% on past projects, exceeding the required threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To guarantee seamless integration with existing systems such as civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories, you propose using our API integration capabilities, specifically leveraging API gateways like Kong, message brokers like Apache Kafka, and identity providers like Active Directory / LDAP or Keycloak. our experience with GED systems like Alfresco and Maarch Courrier will also be beneficial for integrating with EDM systems. For hosting on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, our have experience with cloud providers like Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud, which are European suppliers and meet the requirement of no dependency on non-European suppliers. our can leverage our expertise in containerisation using Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm to ensure efficient deployment and management of the infrastructure. To ensure high performance and low latency, you propose designing a cloud-native architecture that takes advantage of auto-scaling, load balancing, and caching mechanisms. our experience with Terraform and Ansible as IaC tools will help in creating a scalable and secure infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, to mitigate the legacy API integration risk, which is considered medium, you recommend conducting a thorough SI audit before designing the integration architecture. a thorough SI audit will help identify potential risks and ensure a smooth integration process. Overall, our current technology stack and expertise can meet the requirements, and with careful design and planning, we can propose an architecture that ensures seamless integration, high performance, and high availability while meeting the security and infrastructure requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires strict GDPR compliance, with data hosted exclusively in the EU, no transfer outside the EU, and sensitive data protected through encryption or anonymization. The solution must also provide explicability and transparency for recommendations and proposals. Given The City of Belval security certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with the EU regulatory frameworks as of 2024, what are the key security and compliance risks associated with this tender, and how can The City of Belval ensure that The City of Belval bid response addresses the key security and compliance risks associated with this tender?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requirements align with The City of Belval existing GDPR posture, including standard data residency in the EU, cross-border transfer policy prohibiting transfers unless an explicit legal basis exists, and utilization of anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models. The City of Belval ISO 27001 certification, which includes the scope of design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, and The City of Belval appointment of a GDPR Data Protection Officer also support compliance with the key security and compliance risks associated with this tender. Key security and compliance risks associated with this tender include ensuring that all data processing and hosting are confined within the EU, implementing adequate encryption or anonymization for sensitive data, providing explicability and transparency in recommendations and proposals generated by AI systems, and adhering to strict GDPR principles." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address Key security and compliance risks associated with this tender, our bid response should highlight The City of Belval experience with the EU regulatory frameworks such as GDPR, the capability to perform Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) within an average duration of 3 weeks, and The City of Belval use of anonymisation tools for protecting sensitive data. Additionally, The City of Belval must emphasize The City of Belval AI security controls, including prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation, and the security review process for model updates. The City of Belval audit and logging capabilities, with all queries logged and stored in an immutable manner through append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining, along with real-time SIEM integration using tools like Wazuh or Elastic SIEM, will also be crucial in demonstrating The City of Belval ability to monitor and ensure compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By focusing on these aspects and ensuring that The City of Belval data hosting, processing, and AI-driven recommendation systems are transparent, explainable, and compliant with GDPR requirements, The City of Belval can effectively address The City of Belval's requirements and mitigate associated security and compliance risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires compliance with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and a level of security. The solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no automated decisions without explicit agent validation. Given our company's legal standing, procurement experience across EU jurisdictions, IP model, insurance, standard contractual clauses, and AI regulatory posture (GDPR, EU AI Act) as of 2024, what are the key legal risks associated with The tender, and how can our company's ensure that our company's bid response is legally compliant?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, the key legal risks associated with this tenderinclude open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow, EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation. However, given that our company's operations are intra-EU only, cross-border data flow risks are mitigated. To ensure our bid response is legally compliant, our company's must highlight our company's standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) of GDPR for processing personal data, which is performance of a task in public interest. our company's should also emphasize our company's adherence to EU AI Act, ensuring transparency and human oversight in The solution, with no automated decisions without explicit agent validation. our company's default IP model, which transfers all deliverables to the client upon final payment, and our company's source code escrow capability through Logitas (France) can help mitigate vendor lock-in risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company's professional indemnity insurance of 5 million euros and cyber liability insurance of 2 million euros provide a level of security. our company's should also ensure that our bid response complies with the standard contractual clauses our company's typically use, including SLA penalty mechanisms, termination notice periods, data return and destruction obligations, and price revision mechanisms. By addressing these aspects, our company's can demonstrate our company's commitment to legal compliance and risk mitigation, strengthening our company's position in the tender process." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain mastered and compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities. The City of Belval expects an approach that optimizes costs while guaranteeing quality of service. Given our company's financials, active project budgets, daily rates, overhead, cash position, tender eligibility thresholds, and cost sensitivity parameters as of 2024, what is our company's projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our company's can propose to the client?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, I do not have information about the specific costs or expenses associated with the project. The global budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over 4 years, but our company's average annual revenue is approximately 4.2 million euros, and our company's have a target gross margin of 28 percent. To estimate our projected margin on this contract, our company's would need more information about the costs associated with the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, considering our company's minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18 percent, and assuming our company's can maintain a target gross margin of 28 percent, our projected margin on this contract could potentially be around 28 percent of the total contract value, which would be approximately 840,000 euros over the four-year period. Regarding cost-optimization strategies, given our company's cost sensitivity parameters, our company's know that 35 percent of project costs are fixed and 65 percent are variable. our company's can propose strategies such as absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors for minor budget reductions or reducing scope by removing optional modules and reducing training days for more significant budget cuts. Additionally, considering our company's pricing model, which includes standard daily rates for various roles and margins on infrastructure and software licenses, our company's could explore optimizing resource allocation to minimize costs while maintaining the required quality of service. optimizing might involve carefully selecting the project team members based on the project team members daily rates and ensuring that the most cost-effective solutions are chosen for infrastructure and software needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without more specific details about the project expenses and requirements, it's challenging to provide a precise projected margin or tailored cost-optimization strategies." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, I do not have information about the specific costs or expenses associated with the project you're referring to. The global budget for the project you're referring to is estimated at 3 million euros over 4 years, but our company's average annual revenue is approximately 4.2 million euros, and our company's have a target gross margin of 28 percent. To estimate our company's projected margin on this contract, our company's would need more information about the costs associated with the project you're referring to." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, considering our company's minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18 percent, and assuming our company's can maintain a target gross margin of 28 percent, our projected margin on this contract could potentially be around 28 percent of the total contract value, which would be approximately 840,000 euros over the four-year period. Regarding cost-optimization strategies, given our company's cost sensitivity parameters, our company's know that 35 percent of project costs are fixed and 65 percent are variable. our company's can propose strategies such as absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors for minor budget reductions or reducing scope by removing optional modules and reducing training days for more significant budget cuts. Additionally, considering our company's pricing model, which includes standard daily rates for various roles and margins on infrastructure and software licenses, our company's could explore optimizing resource allocation to minimize costs while maintaining the required quality of service. optimizing might involve carefully selecting the project team members based on the project team members daily rates and ensuring that the most cost-effective solutions are chosen for infrastructure and software needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without more specific details about the project you're referring to expenses and requirements, it's challenging to provide a precise projected margin or tailored cost-optimization strategies. Based on the provided context, I do not have information about the specific costs or expenses associated with the project you're referring to. the provided context does not mention a project with a global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, and therefore, I cannot estimate our company's projected margin on this contract. Regarding cost-optimization strategies, according to our cost sensitivity parameters, our company's have defined impacts for budget reductions: absorb via rate renegotiation with subcontractors for a 10 percent reduction, scope reduction by removing optional modules and reducing training days for a 20 percent reduction." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without specific details about the project you're referring to expenses and requirements, I cannot propose tailored cost-optimization strategies. our company's context provides information on our company's pricing model, including standard daily rates and target gross margin percentage, but without knowing how standard daily rates and target gross margin percentage apply to the project you're referring to, I cannot provide further guidance on optimizing costs while guaranteeing quality of service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires an intelligent assistance tool that can facilitate access to information, improve quality of answers, reduce processing times, and provide explicability and transparency for recommendations and proposals. Given our company's LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, performance benchmarks, past AI use cases, and known trade-offs as of 2024, what AI components and innovation strategy can our company's propose to meet these requirements, and how can our company's ensure that our company's solution is aligned with the client's expectations? To address The City of Belval needs for an intelligent assistance tool, our company's can leverage our company's LLM stack, particularly our company's preferred sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong French-language performance and is self-hostable.  our company's propose combining our preferred sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong French-language performance and is self-hostable with our company's RAG capabilities to provide accurate and up-to-date information retrieval from The City of Belval knowledge base, utilizing strategies like dense vector semantic search or hybrid approaches for optimal results." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For fine-tuning, our company's can apply methods such as LoRA or full fine-tune on a domain-specific corpus to adapt our preferred sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong French-language performance and is self-hostable to The City of Belval tone and format requirements, aiming for an average accuracy gain of 12%. To ensure explicability and transparency, our company's will implement XAI methods including source citation through RAG grounding, chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring. our company's low-confidence threshold is set at 0.65, triggering an uncertainty warning and escalation to human supervisors when necessary. our company's past AI use cases in public administration, such as the regulatory document Q&A assistant, demonstrate our company's capability to deliver relevant solutions. our company's will build on this experience to tailor our company's approach to The City of Belval specific needs. To align with client expectations and ensure compliance with EU AI regulations, our company's emphasize our company's commitment to transparency, explicability, and data privacy, avoiding real-time learning from user data and instead opting for quarterly offline fine-tuning on anonymized datasets.  our company's innovation strategy involves ongoing research into knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, which could enhance the tool's capabilities over time. our company's will monitor our solution performance against benchmarks like retrieval precision at 5 (targeting above 0.87) and answer relevance score (aiming for above 0.84), with a focus on minimizing hallucination rates." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By proposing a tailored AI solution that integrates our company's strengths in LLMs, RAG, fine-tuning, and XAI, while being mindful of known trade-offs such as model size vs energy consumption and explicability vs performance, we can meet The City of Belval requirements for an intelligent assistance tool that is both effective and transparent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to limit The City of Belval environmental footprint by reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact. Given our company's EcoVadis rating, carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs as of 2024, what CSR and sustainability posture can our company's propose to support The City of Belval objectives, and how can our company's ensure that our company's solution contributes to reducing the environmental impact of The City of Belval systems of information? As the CSR & Sustainability Officer for Nexus Engineering S.r.l., the CSR & Sustainability Officer for Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can propose a comprehensive CSR and sustainability posture to support the client's objectives. our company's has achieved a Silver EcoVadis rating with a score of 62, demonstrating our company's commitment to sustainability. our company's have also conducted a Bilan Carbone in 2023, which reported a total scope 1 and 2 greenhouse gas emission of 148 tCO2e." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To reduce energetic consumption and rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact, our company's can leverage our company's green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and powered by 100% renewable energy. our green hosting partners, OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and powered by 100% renewable energy Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) ratings are 1.3 and 1.28, respectively, indicating efficient energy use. our company's digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and green IT hardware procurement policy, can help reduce energy consumption by an estimated 35% compared to our company's baseline. our company's can also implement these practices for the City's systems of information. In terms of social commitments, our company's prioritize gender equality, with a gender equality index of 88, and promote diversity by having 4.2% of our company's workforce comprised of disabled workers. our company's also prefer local subcontracting and adhere to accessibility standards such as WCAG 2.1 AA and RGAA 4.1. our company's AI ethics principles ensure that our company's solutions are designed with human oversight, transparency, and fairness in mind. our company's publish an ethics charter and conduct quarterly bias testing to prevent discriminatory outputs. However, our company's acknowledge potential sustainability trade-offs, such as the tension between high availability and energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address potential sustainability trade-offs, such as the tension between high availability and energy consumption, our company's can implement low-power standby modes with wake-up times under 90 seconds, which is compatible with our company's SLA requirements. By proposing a solution that incorporates our company's green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, and AI ethics principles, we can contribute to reducing the environmental impact of the City's systems of information. our company's will also ensure transparency by providing carbon reporting based on GRI Standards (partial) and work towards achieving ISO 14001 certification by 2026. our company's net-zero target for 2040 demonstrates our company's long-term commitment to sustainability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "### Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in collaboration with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. consortium partners, proposes a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. approach integrates AI innovation, security compliance, legal adherence, budget optimization, and sustainability principles to deliver an effective, transparent, and environmentally responsible system. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. leverage Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in Agile Scrum methodology, sovereign cloud hosting, GDPR compliance, and green IT practices to ensure a tailored solution that meets the City of Belval's specific needs. ### Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval's requires an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool must integrate with existing systems, respect regulatory requirements (notably GDPR), ensure data sovereignty, and minimize environmental impact. Key functionalities include assistance with information consultation, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration. ### Proposed Solution a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool utilizes the Mistral 7B Instruct LLM model for strong French-language performance, combined with RAG capabilities for accurate information retrieval from the City of Belval's knowledge base. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. apply fine-tuning methods like LoRA or full fine-tune on a domain-specific corpus to adapt the Mistral 7B Instruct LLM model to the City of Belval's tone and format requirements, aiming for an average accuracy gain of 12%. For explicability and transparency, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. implement XAI methods including source citation through RAG grounding, chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring, with a low-confidence threshold set at 0.65." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure seamless integration, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. use API gateways like Kong, message brokers like Apache Kafka, and identity providers like Active Directory / LDAP or Keycloak. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. hosting solution leverages Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud, European suppliers that meet the sovereignty requirement, with a PUE rating of 1.3 and 1.28, respectively. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. design a cloud-native architecture utilizing containerisation with Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm for efficient deployment and management. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. security posture is grounded in Nexus Engineering S.r.l. ISO 27001 certification and GDPR compliance, with standard data residency in the EU, cross-border transfer policy, and utilization of anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. perform Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) within an average duration of 3 weeks and emphasize AI security controls including prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation, and the security review process for model updates." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "From a legal perspective, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. highlight Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) of GDPR for processing personal data and adherence to the EU AI Act, ensuring transparency and human oversight in Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. default IP model transfers all deliverables to the client upon final payment, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. offer source code escrow capability through Logitas (France). While specific cost details are not provided due to lack of information on project expenses, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. general approach to budget optimization includes absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors for up to a 10% reduction and scope reduction by removing optional modules and reducing training days for up to a 20% reduction. In terms of sustainability, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose leveraging green hosting partners OVHcloud and Scaleway, both powered by 100% renewable energy. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. digital sobriety practices aim to reduce energy consumption by an estimated 35%, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy. ### Unaddressed Requirements Due to the lack of specific cost information related to the project, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. cannot provide detailed financial projections or exact costs for a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. However, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. emphasize Nexus Engineering S.r.l. commitment to transparency and are prepared to work closely with the City of Belval's to develop a comprehensive and tailored budget plan upon receipt of more detailed project requirements. ### Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. consortium partners, is committed to delivering an innovative, secure, compliant, and sustainable artificial intelligence solution for the City of Belval's." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. approach combines cutting-edge technologies with robust methodologies to ensure the development of a tool that not only meets but exceeds the City of Belval's expectations for assisting municipal agents in municipal agents daily activities. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. look forward to the opportunity to collaborate closely with the City of Belval's to tailor Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposal further and address any additional requirements or concerns that may arise during the project development." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval requires improving efficiency of administrative services, quality of service rendered to users, reducing environmental footprint, and minimizing energetic consumption. The proposed solution must integrate into existing practices, provide intelligent assistance, facilitate access to information, improve quality of answers, reduce processing times, and ensure continuity of file processing. Given our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, what is the most suitable project management approach for this tender, and how can our company's ensure a coherent bid response?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

